Hello Maintainers,
Thanks for providing such a great library to the world!

Problem here is about base64 decoding:
    #include <openssl/evp.h>

    int main() {
                unsigned char *str=(unsigned char *)"YQ=="; /* "a" => "YQ==" */
                unsigned char dst[4] = {'\0', '\0', '\0', '\0'};
                int ret = EVP_DecodeBlock(dst, str, (int)strlen((const char *)str));

                printf("dst=%s, ret=%d\n", dst, ret);
    }

In this example, the return value of EVP_DecodeBlock is **3**. I'm expecting **1**.  As you can see, there are two padding equal signs there, according to https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4648#section-4

Could you do me a favor and give me some guidance? I want to know the decoded data's actual length.

comments:
See doc/man3/EVP_EncodeInit.pod

Basically the data is padded.

i.e.
````
EVP_DecodeBlock() will decode the block of B<n> characters of base 64 data
contained in B<f> and store the result in B<t>. Any leading whitespace will be
trimmed as will any trailing whitespace, newlines, carriage returns or EOF
characters. After such trimming the length of the data in B<f> must be divisible
by 4. For every 4 input bytes exactly 3 output bytes will be produced. The
output will be padded with 0 bits if necessary to ensure that the output is
always 3 bytes for every 4 input bytes. This function will return the length of
the data decoded or -1 on error.
````


There is some internal code from another function that does the following:
````
    outlen = EVP_DecodeBlock(outbuf, (unsigned char *)in, inlen);
    if (outlen < 0) {
        ERR_raise(ERR_LIB_CT, CT_R_BASE64_DECODE_ERROR);
        goto err;
    }

    /* Subtract padding bytes from |outlen|.  Any more than 2 is malformed. */
    i = 0;
    while (in[--inlen] == '=') {
        --outlen;
        if (++i > 2)
            goto err;
    }
````

@mattcaswell Hi Matt,
I've tried to draft the test code as below; the result is correct. Thank you so much!
```
#include <openssl/evp.h>
void base64decode()
{
    unsigned char *src = (unsigned char *)"YQ==";
    unsigned char dst[8];
    int dlen;
    EVP_ENCODE_CTX *ctx = EVP_ENCODE_CTX_new();
    EVP_DecodeInit(ctx);
    EVP_DecodeUpdate(ctx, dst, &dlen, src, (int)strlen((const char *)src));
    OPENSSL_assert(dlen == 1);
    OPENSSL_assert(dst[0] == (unsigned char)'a');
    EVP_DecodeFinal(ctx, dst, &dlen);
    OPENSSL_assert(dlen == 0);
    EVP_ENCODE_CTX_free(ctx);
}
```
